From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: keep distribution format checks enabled

Milton unconditionally disables all format diagnostics. This conflicts with
openEuler's -Werror=format-security hardening flag because GCC reports that
format-security cannot remain enabled after -Wno-format.

Remove the blanket suppression and retain the distribution compiler policy.

Patch-Source: downstream adaptation of Milton 1.9.1 CMakeLists.txt
Patch-License: GPL-3.0-or-later
Upstream-Status: Not Submitted (automated upstream writes forbidden)
---
 CMakeLists.txt | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -55,7 +55,6 @@ if(UNIX)
     -Wno-write-strings
     -Wno-c++11-compat-deprecated-writable-strings
     -Wno-null-dereference
-    -Wno-format
     -fno-strict-aliasing
     -fno-omit-frame-pointer
     -Wno-extern-c-compat
--
2.50.1
